# sample OPLS1999 AGBNP parameter file for distribution with libagbnp. 
#
# ideal alpha from fitting small Born radius tail of mkws LJ energies.
# gamma and alpha corrections from small molecule data  
#
# radius = defines dielectric cavity, used also for surface area
# igamma, ialpha, idelta = non-polar parameters
# sgamma, salpha, sdelta = correction parameters
#
# non-polar and correction energies have the same functional form
#
#  Sum_i gamma_i A_i + alpha_i a_i/(B_i+Rw)^3
#
#   a_i     = - 16 pi rho epsilon_iw sigma_iw^6/3
#   espilon_iw = sqrt(epsilon_i epsilon_w)
#   sigma_iw = sqrt(sigma_i sigma_w)
#   epsilon_w = 0.155 kcal/mol
#   sigma_w = 3.15365 Ang
#   rho = 0.033428 Ang^-3
#   Rw = 1.4
#
#  mostly radius = sigma/2
#
#type  radius   igamma   ialpha   idelta  sgamma   salpha     sdelta   GBdistcorr
